 "doc": "Rules of the sheet stage (docs/realistic-anatomy.md section 7.2.2, WP RS2), held as data; every number is a named parameter. reseg.py `sheets` reads SEED tips only; no number here was chosen from a held-out tip, and none was changed after a score had been computed. `filter` is the sheetness filter and the cutting of its medial surface into candidates. A candidate is NAMED for a lamella only when exactly one candidate per side meets every rule (passers of a sheet within `merge_gap_mm` of each other, and, where `merge_angle_deg` is given, with plate normals within that angle, count as one lamella; `dominance_ratio` is the septum's extra condition); otherwise the lamella is unassigned and every candidate's per-rule scores go to incoming/_rs/sheets-report.json. Distances are mm in the working volume's RAS frame (+r is the patient's right). An `end` is the extreme `end_fraction` of a candidate's voxels along the stated axis; `roi` bounds the candidate's centroid (|r|, a, s); a `probe` looks along the plate normal, up to `probe_mm` each way; `late` rules (the expensive ones) are evaluated only when the earlier rules pass.",
